---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title={SITE_NAME}
  description="Design engineer who owns the finish layer."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-2xl tracking-tight text-pretty sm:text-3xl sm:leading-snug">
    <h1 class="enter">
      Hello.
      <br />
      I'm Jamie Thompson, a design engineer who cares about easing curves, color
      ramps, and frontend craft the way some people care about sports.
    </h1>
    <p class="enter mt-6" style="--stagger: 1">
      I've spent my career owning the finish layer — visual and interactive
      details — of products, and building design systems from the ground up that
      hold the bar for a team.
    </p>
    <p class="enter mt-6" style="--stagger: 2">
      Right now that's Lacquer, a design system for finished AI-generated UI.{" "}
      <span class="text-muted-foreground">
        Every component has a written contract, is built from that contract,
        graded against it before it ships, and regraded by CI on every PR after.
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="enter mt-6" style="--stagger: 3">
      The background of this page is the other kind of thing I make.{" "}
      <span class="text-muted-foreground">
        It's a field of code drawn on the GPU: 25 fps while the light moves, 60
        fps when you click, none once you leave it alone. I wrote up how.
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="enter mt-6" style="--stagger: 4">
      I also design interiors. Different material, same job.{" "}
      <span class="text-muted-foreground">
        Have a point of view and carry it all the way to the finish.
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="enter mt-6" style="--stagger: 5">
      Nice to meet you.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
